// ROADMAP A16 prerequisite (2026-09-09): MORE THAN 512 FUNCTIONS.
// The fn cap was raised 512 -> 560, and raising it exposed a defect that would
// otherwise have shipped silently: fntab[2200+i] (b1_facts, the per-fn planning
// facts) is indexed by FN INDEX and was sized 512, so fn 512..514 wrote straight
// through the b1_scratch cells at 2712/2713/2714 -- the B1 call-site counter and
// the skip-save flag -- which is a WRONG `bl` TARGET, not a wrong value.
// NO OTHER GATE CAN CATCH THIS: every other construct, kernel and std_test is far
// under 512 fns, so the cap was never exercised by anything. That is why this
// construct is deliberately large. main() calls fns at indices 513, 519 and 0, so
// the b1_facts entries that used to alias b1_scratch are the ones under test.
// b1_scratch now lives at 2764..2766, leaving b1_facts 2200..2763 = 564 cells.
// EXPECT 1035 from: hand: 521 functions (ROADMAP A16)
fn m0(x: i64) -> i64 { x + 0 }
fn m1(x: i64) -> i64 { x + 1 }
fn m2(x: i64) -> i64 { x + 2 }
fn m3(x: i64) -> i64 { x + 3 }
fn m4(x: i64) -> i64 { x + 4 }
